      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/postcard-2014-20140501_17292815_0170.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140501_17292815_0170&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/postcard-2014-20140501_17292815_0170.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/postcard-2014-20140501_17293599_0171.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140501_17293599_0171&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/postcard-2014-20140501_17293599_0171.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From: Jessie Webster, To: Bess Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Mailed From: Pleasantville, Illinois on April 15, 1911&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Miss Bess Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Pearl, Illinois&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dear Bess;&lt;br&gt;
How have you been getting along? I guess you got through all right. It is too bad Leta failed on grammar. You and Opal had better come over when Leta comes. I got through all right.&lt;br&gt;
Lovingly,&lt;br&gt;
Jessie Webster&lt;/p&gt;</description>
